   "kind": "approximation (over-kill), CONFIRMED BY CANARY",
   "text": "N7's graph-level proxies over-kill. Trump's own contact graph CONTAINS a 4-cycle, so the N7a proxy would remove the known optimum. This is exactly the realizability caveat A25 recorded, now demonstrated on a realized packing. N7a/N7d are report-only columns and must never be composed. Note also that N7d's extra condition -- \"tilt classes admit a common assignment in (18,45) deg\" -- is VACUOUS at this resolution: any acyclic orientation of a 4-cycle is realisable by 4 distinct tilt values inside any open interval, so N7d reduces to \"some 4-cycle has all four links corner-on-edge\"."
  },
  {
   "id": "G-A43-5",
