 "findings": [
  "FIELD: the A39 resealed guard field was used (artifact + standalone PASS report both present). eta_cert = 2518483/6250000 = 0.40295728 EXACTLY, so the W1 threshold is 1 + eta = 8768483/6250000 = 1.40295728 and the W2 threshold is 2 + eta = 15018483/6250000 = 2.40295728. The A33 fallback (eta = 0.425399552) was not needed. The field is exactly D4-closed (0 defects over 1468 atoms).",
  "REGRESSION PASS. With the new filters off, every number in A31 level0_k{3..7}.json (cum, marg, soft, branch, Ehist, Burnside rows) reproduces EXACTLY, and the Level-1 weighted geometric-mean decoration counts reproduce A31 exactly at every k (271, 1.733e4, 2.179e6, 3.298e8, 4.095e10). The refitted k=11 composed totals reproduce A31 headline to the digit: 4.153e29 / 3.255e30 / 2.223e30.",
  "N1 (per-wall <= 3) is the ONLY member of the 2026 library that bites at Level 0, and it is now a HARD row (R11). Keep-factor on MAIN: {3: 1.0, 4: 0.9357, 5: 0.8822, 6: 0.8097, 7: 0.7398}. It weakens as k grows only slowly and is worth x1.35 at k=7.",
  "N5 (W1 tight-variety) and N6 (W2 pair tight-sum) are EXACT and kill NOTHING at Level 0: the certified m_low over the centre box of EVERY one of the 9 admissible wall masks (full tilt t in [0,1]) is exactly 0.000000, against the threshold 1.40295728. R12 = R11 at every k. This is a measurement, not a failure: the same field pointwise exempts 7.13%% of admissible (t,cx,cy) grid cells at that threshold, so the kill power exists but a wall-mask window is ~10^6 times too coarse to see it. The guard field needs POSITION information that a combinatorial structure does not carry.",
  "COMPOSED EXACT count MAIN' = MAIN & N1 & N5 & N6 (= MAIN & N1, since N5/N6 are inert): {3: 10, 4: 131, 5: 2007, 6: 33967, 7: 623194} at k = 3..7. Non-thin: {3: 1, 4: 17, 5: 245, 6: 4001, 7: 67130}.",
  "HEADLINE: the whole 2026 theorem library buys a factor of about 2 on the k=11 structure count. Composed EXACT k=11 projection {'M1_exp': '2.304e+29', 'M2_logquad': '1.507e+30', 'M3_ratio_lin': '1.087e+30'} versus A31 4.15e29 / 3.26e30 / 2.22e30. MAIN' non-thin gives {'M1_exp': '2.733e+28', 'M2_logquad': '3.473e+28', 'M3_ratio_lin': '3.327e+28'}. A31's GO/NO-GO verdict is unchanged: an enumerate-then-solve structure-first campaign at k=11 remains non-viable.",
  "N2 (A38.1 all-wall kill) at the k=11 JOIN: the all-wall share of MAIN&N1 decays exponentially in k ({'3': 0.7, '4': 0.4656, '5': 0.2417, '6': 0.0956, '7': 0.0314}), fit log frac = 2.2270 - 0.7795 k, extrapolating to 1.75e-03 at k=11. So the one place where N2 is a legitimate hard kill it removes about 0.2% of the k=11 graph count. There is also an exact combinatorial squeeze: under N1 the four walls carry at most 12 square-wall incidences, so an all-wall k=11 core has at most ONE corner square.",
  "N3 (A21 THM3) at the k=11 JOIN: two thirds of tilt-feasible decorations already carry a zero-pinned tilt class (a wall-flush edge forces phi = 0, which satisfies THM3 for free). The no-zero-class share is FLAT in k ({'3': 0.3557, '4': 0.3454, '5': 0.3406, '6': 0.3369, '7': 0.3358}) and extrapolates to 0.314 at k=11, so THM3 can bite on at most ~31% of decorated k=11 structures -- and only on the subset of those in which the tilt system FORCES all 11 tilts into (18,27)u(63,72) deg, which this census does not test. THM3 is not a bulk filter.",
  "N4 (Maxwell flush-mandatory) is CONDITIONAL, not certified -- the provenance check contradicts the A43 brief (structure_lemmas.md marks m >= 3k+1 SOFT and A32-H1 ruled it unusable). Two measurements: (i) at Level 0 the column 2E >= 3k+1 is IMPLIED by non-thinness -- min total degree 3 gives 2E >= 3k and at least one wall edge gives 2E >= 3k+1 -- which is why MAIN'&N4&non-thin equals MAIN'&non-thin at every k; (ii) at Level 1 the flush-mandatory share of decorations collapses with k ({'3': 0.1354, '4': 0.0533, '5': 0.0314, '6': 0.025, '7': 0.0072}), extrapolating to 6.3e-04 at k=11. If Maxwell were ever proved, the composed k=11 total would fall to {'M1_exp': '1.634e+26', 'M2_logquad': '8.933e+26', 'M3_ratio_lin': '6.909e+26'}, and with non-thinness to {'M1_exp': '1.716e+25', 'M2_logquad': '2.181e+25', 'M3_ratio_lin': '2.090e+25'} -- i.e. to A31's own best case of ~2.5e25. Maxwell is the single biggest available lever and it is the one that is unproven.",
  "N7 (wastage motifs) OVER-KILLS THE KNOWN OPTIMUM: Trump's contact graph contains a 4-cycle, so the N7a proxy would delete the realized packing. The proxy share of MAIN grows fast with k ({3: 0.0, 4: 0.0929, 5: 0.2993, 6: 0.5206, 7: 0.6899}) and at Level 1 the all-corner-on-edge 4-cycle share reaches 0.44 weighted / 0.96 median at k=7, so it LOOKS like the strongest filter available and is in fact unsound as stated. A23/A25 kill specific certified CELLS, not graph motifs; the realizability caveat A25 recorded is now demonstrated on a realized packing.",
  "N5 DOES bite at Level 1, partially. On the wall-flush pinned window (tilt exactly 0, centre exactly 1/2 from the wall, along-wall coordinate free) the certified m_low runs from 1.013644 to 1.437085 against the threshold 1.402957, and 36 of 2000 slabs -- 1.8%% of the along-wall range -- are certified EXEMPT, identically on all four walls. So W1 does not forbid wall-flush contacts, but it does forbid 1.8%% of their positions. This is the only place in the census where the guard field actually cuts, and it cuts only because the decoration pins two of the three placement coordinates.",
  "TRUMP CANARY PASS (20/20 checks). Wall degrees 3/3/3/2 exactly meet the new N1 cap; 3 squares are interior so N2 correctly does not fire; max exact coverage 1.137624852 vs threshold 1.402957280 (slack 0.265); worst exact pair sum 2.207686884 vs 2.402957280; total coverage 11.375094588 vs total field mass 11.402957280 (slack 0.0279); no Trump placement lies in an exempt eroded grid cell (A38 canary cross-check).",
  "INDEPENDENT CROSS-CHECK of A31 Level 1: a wall-edge-resolved re-enumeration (each square-wall edge chosen flush or corner independently, with the phi = 0 versus phi != 0 consistency constraint) reproduces A31's wall-CLASS enumeration exactly -- ratio 1.000 on every sampled graph at every k. A31's decoration count was suspected of under-counting the 2^Esw wall menu; it does not.",
  "BOTTOM LINE for the PI bulk-kill thesis: no certified theorem proven since A31 bulk-kills structures. Each one fails for a different structural reason -- N2/N3 are EXISTENTIAL and therefore vacuous on a k<11 core; N5/N6 are POSITIONAL and a contact structure carries no position; N4 is UNPROVEN; N7 is UNSOUND as a motif filter (it kills Trump). Only N1, which was already computed as a soft column in A31, survives as a hard prune, and it is worth x1.35 at k=7. The composed exact k=11 count moves from 4.15e29 to 2.30e29."
 ]
